<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilgamesh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 2700 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/28th-century-bce">28th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gilgamesh was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-dynastic-period">Early Dynastic period</a>, perhaps around 2700 BCE, who became the hero of the oldest great epic of world literature. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list">Sumerian King List</a> names him as a ruler of Uruk, and later tradition credited him with building the city's walls. Sumerian poems and the Akkadian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epic-of-gilgamesh">Epic of Gilgamesh</a> tell of his friendship with Enkidu and his search for immortality, though no contemporary inscription confirms his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gilgamesh.jpg" alt="Gilgamesh" width="320" height="747" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hero_lion_Dur-Sharrukin_Louvre_AO19862.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
